{"parentUuid":"9b7ce073-6578-4e47-a1bb-e267e73b4f21","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a762a63df072879b5","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg22YcbyJn6CXz3FzTRmV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013KHMo3pW627cRGBvyycowD","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\mes_guide.txt","offset":1000,"limit":94},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_read_input_tokens":70977,"output_tokens":202,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":37},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":724},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":202,"cache_read_input_tokens":70977,"cache_creation_input_tokens":724,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":724,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013KHMo3pW627cRGBvyycowD":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\mes_guide.txt","offset":1000,"limit":94}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9b7d5a11-8989-4d75-bf13-a52254b633c6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg22YcN5846p7KRb6qK5V","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4bf8508e-f569-4474-a4c2-5564efa88216","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:10:48.998Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"4bf8508e-f569-4474-a4c2-5564efa88216","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"a762a63df072879b5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013KHMo3pW627cRGBvyycowD","type":"tool_result","content":"1000\tStep 8: Now we can enter the new injector code. We simply type bv742dv5u\n1001\tfrom the keyboard (or we can use the mouse and change each character).\n1002\t\n1003\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 52 of 63\n1004\t\fThen we press \"Enter\" key to go to next step (or we click on the OK button).\n1005\tWe can also press button Cancel and abort the procedure.\n1006\t\n1007\tStep 8: Now the system will ask you to confirm that the data you entered is\n1008\tcorrect.\n1009\tYou can press Y to go to next step and write the new code in the engine control\n1010\tmodule.\n1011\tYou can also press N to abort the procedure.\n1012\t\n1013\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 53 of 63\n1014\t\fAfter you press Y the system will start writing the new code to the engine control\n1015\tmodule.\n1016\t\n1017\tThe procedure may fail here if the new code is not correct.\n1018\t\n1019\tMultiecuscan User Guide                                      Page 54 of 63\n1020\t\fStep 9: Now you can go to parameters and check the value of \"Injector code Cyl.\n1021\t3\".\n1022\t\n1023\tStep 10: Disconnect from engine control module. You can disconnect from the\n1024\tcontrol module and return to Multiecuscan main screen by pressing F11.\n1025\t\n1026\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 55 of 63\n1027\t\f6. Connect to PROXI Alignment and activate Cruise Control light\n1028\ton Fiat Stilo\n1029\t\n1030\tIn this example we will connect to Fiat Stilo and use the PROXI Alignment\n1031\tprocedure settings to enable Cruise control light on dashboard.\n1032\t\n1033\tStep 1: Connect the interface to the computer and to the OBD port of the vehicle.\n1034\t\n1035\tStep 2: Select make, model, version and control module.\n1036\t\n1037\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 56 of 63\n1038\t\fStep 3: Click button \"Connect\" (or press F10 on your keyboard). Multiecuscan will\n1039\tstart connecting to your car.\n1040\tAfter successful connection Multiecuscan will show the Info screen.\n1041\tIn this example the car is configured properly and doesn't need to be aligned. So,\n1042\tthe system will warn us that PROXI Alignment is not needed.\n1043\tWe can just press Y and continue.\n1044\t\n1045\tStep 4: Press F7 to go to the Adjustments screen.\n1046\t\n1047\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 57 of 63\n1048\t\fStep 5: Select \"Cruise control light\" and press F10 to execute this adjustment.\n1049\tThe system will show current value of the setting.\n1050\t\n1051\tStep 6: Change the value to `Enabled' and press Enter (or click OK).\n1052\t\n1053\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 58 of 63\n1054\t\fStep 7: The system will confirm that operation is complete.\n1055\t\n1056\tStep 8: Now we have to execute the PROXI Alignment procedure to write the\n1057\tnew settings to the car.\n1058\tSo, we select \"PROXI ALIGNMENT PROCEDURE\" and press F10.\n1059\tThe system will ask you to confirm that you want to continue.\n1060\t\n1061\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 59 of 63\n1062\t\fStep 9: After we confirm that we want to continue by pressing Y Multiecuscan will\n1063\tstart the procedure.\n1064\tWhen the process finishes the system will show the status (success or failure).\n1065\t\n1066\tStep 10: After successful execution the system will ask you to turn car's key to\n1067\tOFF position.\n1068\tThat is all. Now the Cruise control light should be enabled and working properly\n1069\twhen you switch ON the cruise control.\n1070\t\n1071\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 60 of 63\n1072\t\f7. Send diagnostic report to Multiecuscan server\n1073\t\n1074\tThe diagnostic reports help us to find and fix problems in Multiecuscan. The\n1075\treport contains information about your last connection (the data sent/received to\n1076\tyour car). It does not contain any personal information or any information about\n1077\tyour computer.\n1078\tMultiecuscan shows a small red button \"Send Report\" on the bottom right part of\n1079\tMultiecuscan main window. The button appears after you disconnect from a\n1080\tcontrol module or after failed connection.\n1081\t\n1082\tStep 1: Connect to a control module.\n1083\t\n1084\tStep 2: Go to errors, parameters, etc.\n1085\t\n1086\tMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 61 of 63\n1087\t\fMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 62 of 63\n1088\t\fStep 3: Disconnect from the control module by pressing F11.\n1089\t\n1090\tStep 4: Click on the red \"Send Report\" button. Your computer has to be\n1091\tconnected to the internet when doing this.\n1092\tThe system will ask you for confirmation. Press Y to confirm.\n1093\t"}]},"uuid":"8452a039-7a1a-483e-a358-9a685495cc31","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:10:49.123Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-User\\7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17\\scratchpad\\mes_guide.txt","content":"Step 8: Now we can enter the new injector code. We simply type bv742dv5u\nfrom the keyboard (or we can use the mouse and change each character).\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 52 of 63\n\fThen we press \"Enter\" key to go to next step (or we click on the OK button).\nWe can also press button Cancel and abort the procedure.\n\nStep 8: Now the system will ask you to confirm that the data you entered is\ncorrect.\nYou can press Y to go to next step and write the new code in the engine control\nmodule.\nYou can also press N to abort the procedure.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 53 of 63\n\fAfter you press Y the system will start writing the new code to the engine control\nmodule.\n\nThe procedure may fail here if the new code is not correct.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide                                      Page 54 of 63\n\fStep 9: Now you can go to parameters and check the value of \"Injector code Cyl.\n3\".\n\nStep 10: Disconnect from engine control module. You can disconnect from the\ncontrol module and return to Multiecuscan main screen by pressing F11.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 55 of 63\n\f6. Connect to PROXI Alignment and activate Cruise Control light\non Fiat Stilo\n\nIn this example we will connect to Fiat Stilo and use the PROXI Alignment\nprocedure settings to enable Cruise control light on dashboard.\n\nStep 1: Connect the interface to the computer and to the OBD port of the vehicle.\n\nStep 2: Select make, model, version and control module.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 56 of 63\n\fStep 3: Click button \"Connect\" (or press F10 on your keyboard). Multiecuscan will\nstart connecting to your car.\nAfter successful connection Multiecuscan will show the Info screen.\nIn this example the car is configured properly and doesn't need to be aligned. So,\nthe system will warn us that PROXI Alignment is not needed.\nWe can just press Y and continue.\n\nStep 4: Press F7 to go to the Adjustments screen.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 57 of 63\n\fStep 5: Select \"Cruise control light\" and press F10 to execute this adjustment.\nThe system will show current value of the setting.\n\nStep 6: Change the value to `Enabled' and press Enter (or click OK).\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 58 of 63\n\fStep 7: The system will confirm that operation is complete.\n\nStep 8: Now we have to execute the PROXI Alignment procedure to write the\nnew settings to the car.\nSo, we select \"PROXI ALIGNMENT PROCEDURE\" and press F10.\nThe system will ask you to confirm that you want to continue.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 59 of 63\n\fStep 9: After we confirm that we want to continue by pressing Y Multiecuscan will\nstart the procedure.\nWhen the process finishes the system will show the status (success or failure).\n\nStep 10: After successful execution the system will ask you to turn car's key to\nOFF position.\nThat is all. Now the Cruise control light should be enabled and working properly\nwhen you switch ON the cruise control.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 60 of 63\n\f7. Send diagnostic report to Multiecuscan server\n\nThe diagnostic reports help us to find and fix problems in Multiecuscan. The\nreport contains information about your last connection (the data sent/received to\nyour car). It does not contain any personal information or any information about\nyour computer.\nMultiecuscan shows a small red button \"Send Report\" on the bottom right part of\nMultiecuscan main window. The button appears after you disconnect from a\ncontrol module or after failed connection.\n\nStep 1: Connect to a control module.\n\nStep 2: Go to errors, parameters, etc.\n\nMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 61 of 63\n\fMultiecuscan User Guide  Page 62 of 63\n\fStep 3: Disconnect from the control module by pressing F11.\n\nStep 4: Click on the red \"Send Report\" button. Your computer has to be\nconnected to the internet when doing this.\nThe system will ask you for confirmation. Press Y to confirm.\n","numLines":94,"startLine":1000,"totalLines":1095}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4bf8508e-f569-4474-a4c2-5564efa88216","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
