{"parentUuid":"dad3c7de-c574-4b9b-b06a-6adb74c9157b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a762a63df072879b5","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg22ZbL6Aufc6uG1MLwdi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UvW62vxekKaZGX7Gz2wRcF","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Multiecuscan Giulia Stelvio paddle shift North American European mode coding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2065,"cache_read_input_tokens":73607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2065,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UvW62vxekKaZGX7Gz2wRcF":{"query":"Multiecuscan Giulia Stelvio paddle shift North American European mode coding"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee4aef1f-813a-4f7e-b5dd-e26d32d62a7c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg22ZZwWc6U8vBh5BFPzP","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bd57507b-8e4e-4b8e-b0e3-939331cf9c5d","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:11:00.294Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"bd57507b-8e4e-4b8e-b0e3-939331cf9c5d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a762a63df072879b5","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg22ZbL6Aufc6uG1MLwdi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H3JjS7HNXs7j1Xr1aSkt7C","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Giulia Stelvio \"manual mode\" paddle shifters revert to automatic Multiecuscan TCM coding"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2065,"cache_read_input_tokens":73607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2065,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01H3JjS7HNXs7j1Xr1aSkt7C":{"query":"Giulia Stelvio \"manual mode\" paddle shifters revert to automatic Multiecuscan TCM coding"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee4aef1f-813a-4f7e-b5dd-e26d32d62a7c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cg22ZZwWc6U8vBh5BFPzP","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b94b50f4-8190-4414-a2d0-672a9fd84224","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:11:00.826Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"bd57507b-8e4e-4b8e-b0e3-939331cf9c5d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"a762a63df072879b5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UvW62vxekKaZGX7Gz2wRcF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Multiecuscan Giulia Stelvio paddle shift North American European mode coding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Paddle shifter behavior Stelvio Quad\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/paddle-shifter-behavior-stelvio-quad.22881/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Giulia/ Stelvio USA to Euro spec paddle shifting mod! General proxy alignment DIY free - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KNlF1RB4P1Y\"},{\"title\":\"Paddle shift retrofit - 2.2 Speciale\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/paddle-shift-retrofit-2-2-speciale.1211508/\"},{\"title\":\"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/\"},{\"title\":\"Does the \\\"Euro spec paddle shifting mod\\\" work in a QV?\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/does-the-euro-spec-paddle-shifting-mod-work-in-a-qv.64568/\"},{\"title\":\"Multiecuscan (MES) - Popular Settings Compilation - Electronics - Giulia Tech Community\",\"url\":\"https://giuliatech.com/t/multiecuscan-mes-popular-settings-compilation/80\"},{\"title\":\"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/page-7\"},{\"title\":\"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/page-4\"},{\"title\":\"Neutral with the paddles\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/neutral-with-the-paddles.18171/\"},{\"title\":\"DIY, add paddle shifters.\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/diy-add-paddle-shifters.44122/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about using Multiecuscan to modify paddle shift behavior between North American and European modes on Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**The Difference Between North American and European Modes:**\n\nNorth American (NAFTA) Giulias with paddle shifters do not have the full functionality seen in non-NAFTA regions. Specifically, pulling on both pedals doesn't shift into neutral, and once in neutral pulling on the right paddle doesn't get you back in drive.\n\n**How to Modify Using Multiecuscan:**\n\nWith MES 4.8 you can switch to the Euro paddle functionality by changing byte 156 from \"50\" to \"40\" then performing a PROXI ALIGNMENT.\n\nMore specifically, in the Body → CAN Setup section, byte 156 bits 4-5 need bitwise calculation: EU version uses xx00xxxx while US version uses xx01xxxx, and PROXI alignment is needed.\n\n**Results:**\n\nUsing MES to alter the PROXI Alignment enables the Euro Spec paddle shifting mod, which means you can pull both paddles to place the gearbox into neutral.\n\n**Compatibility:**\n\nThe modification works on the Stelvio as well as the Giulia, and all you have to do is change byte 156 from 50 to 40.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4d894c32-7019-49f5-8913-2da5c9c8c1b3","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:11:07.115Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Multiecuscan Giulia Stelvio paddle shift North American European mode coding","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YVzmYWxPUVcHJUbMvAtLmW","content":[{"title":"Paddle shifter behavior Stelvio Quad","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/paddle-shifter-behavior-stelvio-quad.22881/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Giulia/ Stelvio USA to Euro spec paddle shifting mod! General proxy alignment DIY free - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KNlF1RB4P1Y"},{"title":"Paddle shift retrofit - 2.2 Speciale","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/paddle-shift-retrofit-2-2-speciale.1211508/"},{"title":"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/"},{"title":"Does the \"Euro spec paddle shifting mod\" work in a QV?","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/does-the-euro-spec-paddle-shifting-mod-work-in-a-qv.64568/"},{"title":"Multiecuscan (MES) - Popular Settings Compilation - Electronics - Giulia Tech Community","url":"https://giuliatech.com/t/multiecuscan-mes-popular-settings-compilation/80"},{"title":"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/page-7"},{"title":"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/page-4"},{"title":"Neutral with the paddles","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/neutral-with-the-paddles.18171/"},{"title":"DIY, add paddle shifters.","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/diy-add-paddle-shifters.44122/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about using Multiecuscan to modify paddle shift behavior between North American and European modes on Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**The Difference Between North American and European Modes:**\n\nNorth American (NAFTA) Giulias with paddle shifters do not have the full functionality seen in non-NAFTA regions. Specifically, pulling on both pedals doesn't shift into neutral, and once in neutral pulling on the right paddle doesn't get you back in drive.\n\n**How to Modify Using Multiecuscan:**\n\nWith MES 4.8 you can switch to the Euro paddle functionality by changing byte 156 from \"50\" to \"40\" then performing a PROXI ALIGNMENT.\n\nMore specifically, in the Body → CAN Setup section, byte 156 bits 4-5 need bitwise calculation: EU version uses xx00xxxx while US version uses xx01xxxx, and PROXI alignment is needed.\n\n**Results:**\n\nUsing MES to alter the PROXI Alignment enables the Euro Spec paddle shifting mod, which means you can pull both paddles to place the gearbox into neutral.\n\n**Compatibility:**\n\nThe modification works on the Stelvio as well as the Giulia, and all you have to do is change byte 156 from 50 to 40."],"durationSeconds":6.803994199991227,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ee4aef1f-813a-4f7e-b5dd-e26d32d62a7c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bd57507b-8e4e-4b8e-b0e3-939331cf9c5d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"b94b50f4-8190-4414-a2d0-672a9fd84224","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"cde09b07-6881-403c-9d9a-f467b27b1473","agentId":"a762a63df072879b5","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H3JjS7HNXs7j1Xr1aSkt7C","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Giulia Stelvio \"manual mode\" paddle shifters revert to automatic Multiecuscan TCM coding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Paddle Shifters ins and outs\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/paddle-shifters-ins-and-outs.47347/\"},{\"title\":\"Paddle shifters - how to switch back to auto D mode after using it\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/paddle-shifters-how-to-switch-back-to-auto-d-mode-after-using-it.15788/\"},{\"title\":\"Paddle shifter behavior Stelvio Quad\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/paddle-shifter-behavior-stelvio-quad.22881/\"},{\"title\":\"Paddle Shifters Honest Question\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/paddle-shifters-honest-question.58861/\"},{\"title\":\"Paddle shifter secret\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/paddle-shifter-secret.8705/page-2\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Giulia (2015)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Giulia_(2015)\"},{\"title\":\"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"},{\"title\":\"Neutral with the paddles\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/neutral-with-the-paddles.18171/\"},{\"title\":\"Shifting into Neutral with Paddles?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/shifting-into-neutral-with-paddles.10365/\"}]\n\nI found information about paddle shifter behavior on Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Let me search for more specific information about Multiecuscan and TCM coding, which are technical tuning tools.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Is Multiecuscan for Alfa Romeo the Right Diagnostic Tool for Your Car?\",\"url\":\"https://www.aliexpress.com/s/wiki-ssr/article/multiecuscan-alfa-romeo\"},{\"title\":\"TCM SOFTWARE\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/tcm-software.1196606/\"},{\"title\":\"Giulia Non QV Race Mode - Multiecuscan\",\"url\":\"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=8112\"},{\"title\":\"Multiecuscan Diagnostic SOFTWARE For Alfa Romeo\",\"url\":\"https://shop.alfissimo.com/diagnostic-softwarehardware-multiecuscanalfaobd/1600-multiecuscan-diagnostic-software-for-alfa-romeo.html\"},{\"title\":\"Multiecuscan SOFTWARE- Alfa Romeo\",\"url\":\"https://shop.alfissimo.com/diagnostic-softwarehardware-multiecuscanalfaobd/1600-software-only-in-conjunction-with-hardware-purchase-1-license-for-multiecuscan-full-version-1-year-update.html\"},{\"title\":\"Injector Coding using MultiECUScan\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/injector-coding-using-multiecuscan.852530/\"},{\"title\":\"MultiMode manual transmission\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MultiMode_manual_transmission\"},{\"title\":\"Finally! Support from Multiecuscan!\",\"url\":\"https://www.4c-forums.com/threads/finally-support-from-multiecuscan.44970/\"},{\"title\":\"Selespeed\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selespeed\"},{\"title\":\"2018 Alfa Giulia - Proxi Alignment issue` - Multiecuscan\",\"url\":\"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=7784\"}]\n\nLet me search more specifically for the issue about manual mode reverting to automatic with paddle shifters.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Selespeed\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selespeed\"},{\"title\":\"How to switch from manual paddle shifting mode back to automatic mode?\",\"url\":\"https://www.718forum.com/threads/how-to-switch-from-manual-paddle-shifting-mode-back-to-automatic-mode.21090/\"},{\"title\":\"What Are Paddle Shifters and How Do They Work? - In The Garage with CarParts.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.carparts.com/blog/what-are-paddle-shifters-and-how-do-they-work/\"},{\"title\":\"Bestätigen, dass das Teil passt\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/175477986192\"},{\"title\":\"Bestätigen, dass das Teil passt\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/176351357442\"},{\"title\":\"www.ebay.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.com/itm/136201064169\"},{\"title\":\"Confirm this item fits\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.com/itm/175477986192\"},{\"title\":\"Prüfen Sie die Artikelbeschreibung, um zu bestätigen, dass das Teil zu Ihrem Fahrzeug passt\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/156784605383\"},{\"title\":\"Prüfen Sie die Artikelbeschreibung, um zu bestätigen, dass das Teil zu Ihrem Fahrzeug passt\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/186387632098\"},{\"title\":\"Check the item description to confirm this fits your vehicle\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.com/itm/156927982235\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found relevant information about your query regarding Giulia and Stelvio paddle shifter behavior:\n\n## Paddle Shifters Reverting to Automatic\n\nThe transmission will revert to automatic mode by itself after a few seconds if you're using the paddles in Drive mode. More specifically, if you click the left paddle to downshift while in normal drive mode, the transmission takes over again and selects the gear it feels appropriate in a few seconds.\n\n## Manual Mode Behavior\n\nWhen in true manual mode, in manual mode with N and A modes, the transmission will automatically upshift when you hit redline. However, in manual with D mode it will bounce off the redline if you do not upshift yourself.\n\n## Multiecuscan and TCM Coding\n\nRegarding the Multiecuscan TCM coding you mentioned, the search results show that Multiecuscan 4.7 can connect to the Transmission and check what errors are stored, and users have successfully used it to modify transmission-related settings. However, I did not find specific information about using Multiecuscan to prevent manual mode from reverting to automatic with paddle shifters.\n\nFor more detailed information about specific TCM coding procedures for your vehicle, you may need to consult Alfa Romeo forums or technical documentation specific to your model year and transmission configuration.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ac084f5e-290c-4917-bab3-305a735fadfb","timestamp":"2026-10-14T11:11:11.523Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Giulia Stelvio \"manual mode\" paddle shifters revert to automatic Multiecuscan TCM coding","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01AgyUAZMgkzM6McLWq6EduF","content":[{"title":"Paddle Shifters ins and outs","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/paddle-shifters-ins-and-outs.47347/"},{"title":"Paddle shifters - how to switch back to auto D mode after using it","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/paddle-shifters-how-to-switch-back-to-auto-d-mode-after-using-it.15788/"},{"title":"Paddle shifter behavior Stelvio Quad","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/paddle-shifter-behavior-stelvio-quad.22881/"},{"title":"Paddle Shifters Honest Question","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/paddle-shifters-honest-question.58861/"},{"title":"Paddle shifter secret","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/paddle-shifter-secret.8705/page-2"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Giulia (2015)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Giulia_(2015)"},{"title":"Added Neutral to paddle shifters! (EU settings)","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/added-neutral-to-paddle-shifters-eu-settings.56872/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"},{"title":"Neutral with the paddles","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/neutral-with-the-paddles.18171/"},{"title":"Shifting into Neutral with Paddles?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/shifting-into-neutral-with-paddles.10365/"}]},"I found information about paddle shifter behavior on Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Let me search for more specific information about Multiecuscan and TCM coding, which are technical tuning tools.",{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019pmQSqjL19uHg9iDmaWQBT","content":[{"title":"Is Multiecuscan for Alfa Romeo the Right Diagnostic Tool for Your Car?","url":"https://www.aliexpress.com/s/wiki-ssr/article/multiecuscan-alfa-romeo"},{"title":"TCM SOFTWARE","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/tcm-software.1196606/"},{"title":"Giulia Non QV Race Mode - Multiecuscan","url":"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=8112"},{"title":"Multiecuscan Diagnostic SOFTWARE For Alfa Romeo","url":"https://shop.alfissimo.com/diagnostic-softwarehardware-multiecuscanalfaobd/1600-multiecuscan-diagnostic-software-for-alfa-romeo.html"},{"title":"Multiecuscan SOFTWARE- Alfa Romeo","url":"https://shop.alfissimo.com/diagnostic-softwarehardware-multiecuscanalfaobd/1600-software-only-in-conjunction-with-hardware-purchase-1-license-for-multiecuscan-full-version-1-year-update.html"},{"title":"Injector Coding using MultiECUScan","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/injector-coding-using-multiecuscan.852530/"},{"title":"MultiMode manual transmission","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MultiMode_manual_transmission"},{"title":"Finally! Support from Multiecuscan!","url":"https://www.4c-forums.com/threads/finally-support-from-multiecuscan.44970/"},{"title":"Selespeed","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selespeed"},{"title":"2018 Alfa Giulia - Proxi Alignment issue` - Multiecuscan","url":"https://www.multiecuscan.net/forum/viewtopic.php?t=7784"}]},"Let me search more specifically for the issue about manual mode reverting to automatic with paddle shifters.",{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018waRDuap4LPSWCvq3dv4Uc","content":[{"title":"Selespeed","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selespeed"},{"title":"How to switch from manual paddle shifting mode back to automatic mode?","url":"https://www.718forum.com/threads/how-to-switch-from-manual-paddle-shifting-mode-back-to-automatic-mode.21090/"},{"title":"What Are Paddle Shifters and How Do They Work? - In The Garage with CarParts.com","url":"https://www.carparts.com/blog/what-are-paddle-shifters-and-how-do-they-work/"},{"title":"Bestätigen, dass das Teil passt","url":"https://www.ebay.de/itm/175477986192"},{"title":"Bestätigen, dass das Teil passt","url":"https://www.ebay.de/itm/176351357442"},{"title":"www.ebay.com","url":"https://www.ebay.com/itm/136201064169"},{"title":"Confirm this item fits","url":"https://www.ebay.com/itm/175477986192"},{"title":"Prüfen Sie die Artikelbeschreibung, um zu bestätigen, dass das Teil zu Ihrem Fahrzeug passt","url":"https://www.ebay.de/itm/156784605383"},{"title":"Prüfen Sie die Artikelbeschreibung, um zu bestätigen, dass das Teil zu Ihrem Fahrzeug passt","url":"https://www.ebay.de/itm/186387632098"},{"title":"Check the item description to confirm this fits your vehicle","url":"https://www.ebay.com/itm/156927982235"}]},"Based on my search results, I found relevant information about your query regarding Giulia and Stelvio paddle shifter behavior:\n\n## Paddle Shifters Reverting to Automatic\n\nThe transmission will revert to automatic mode by itself after a few seconds if you're using the paddles in Drive mode. More specifically, if you click the left paddle to downshift while in normal drive mode, the transmission takes over again and selects the gear it feels appropriate in a few seconds.\n\n## Manual Mode Behavior\n\nWhen in true manual mode, in manual mode with N and A modes, the transmission will automatically upshift when you hit redline. However, in manual with D mode it will bounce off the redline if you do not upshift yourself.\n\n## Multiecuscan and TCM Coding\n\nRegarding the Multiecuscan TCM coding you mentioned, the search results show that Multiecuscan 4.7 can connect to the Transmission and check what errors are stored, and users have successfully used it to modify transmission-related settings. However, I did not find specific information about using Multiecuscan to prevent manual mode from reverting to automatic with paddle shifters.\n\nFor more detailed information about specific TCM coding procedures for your vehicle, you may need to consult Alfa Romeo forums or technical documentation specific to your model year and transmission configuration."],"durationSeconds":10.680563600063325,"searchCount":3},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ee4aef1f-813a-4f7e-b5dd-e26d32d62a7c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b94b50f4-8190-4414-a2d0-672a9fd84224","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
